{% from 'ingressroute.yml.j2' import monitoring_route with context %}
---
{# monitoring_route, not ingressroute(): under Docker this sat on the homepage_private
   isolation net so ONLY homepage could read the unauthenticated private feeds. The
   ClientIP(daniel-server) guard is that isolation's cluster equivalent — homepage still
   runs there, and nothing else on the LAN can fetch the calendars. LAN-only by
   construction (the macro ignores k8s_public_route). #}
{{ monitoring_route(
    container_item.name,
    container_item.hostname | default(container_item.name),
    container_item.port,
  )
}}
{# DECIDED 2026-08-24: the `extra_client_cidrs=['10.42.0.0/16']` that used to be here is GONE,
   and the two callers that needed it now use in-cluster Service DNS instead.

   That CIDR is the whole pod network, so admitting it dissolved the very isolation this route's
   comment claims to provide — "only homepage could read the unauthenticated private feeds"
   became "any pod can". Demonstrated live rather than argued: a GET of /calendar1.ics from a
   source matching only the pod-CIDR clause returned 200 and 847,922 bytes of private calendar.
   The role's own CLAUDE.md still said only Homepage reads these feeds; it did not.

   A NetworkPolicy cannot substitute for this. baseline-ingress admits `app=traefik` on all
   ports and the traefik policy's first ingress rule has no `from:`, so every pod may reach
   Traefik — and traffic arriving through this route carries Traefik's identity regardless of who
   sent it. The route guard IS the control here.

   Narrowing the path was the other obvious fix and buys nothing: this app serves only
   /calendar{1,2,4}.ics, so every path it has is the sensitive content. There is no health
   endpoint to expose instead.

   So both pod callers moved off the edge and onto ClusterIP, where the pod-level NetworkPolicy
   can actually distinguish them:
     - homepage's widgets  -> roles/k8s/homepage/templates/config/services.yaml.j2
     - the Kuma monitor    -> roles/k8s/uptime-kuma/templates/static-monitors.yaml.j2
   The cost is that the Kuma tile no longer exercises the Traefik route, only the app. Accepted:
   nothing reaches this service through the edge any more, so an edge break for ical-proxy has no
   consumer to affect. #}
